==Strategy==
A very simple stage consisting of Those Guys, Mooths to give you a cash boost, Cat Kart itself, and two Dober P.Ds. The enemy combo seems well designed: normally you counter the single target Cat Kart by spamming meatshields, and Dober P.D punishes meatshields with its devastating Wave Attack? Could this...be an actually hard stage?
Well, maybe, until you realise that you can just counter this by only spamming two meatshields. Cat Kart's triple Multi-Hit will kill them off, leaving Dober to attack nothing. In addition, you'll have a lot of money from the intial Mooth as well as the consistent Those Guys spam. In fact, it's very easy to rush this stage and kill Cat Kart before the second Dober even spawns.
At the start, focus on killing Mooth to get as much money as possible before the actual fight starts. Units like [[Lizard Cat (Normal Cat)|either]] [[Crazed Lizard Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Dragon]], [[Crazed Gross Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Gross]], or Gacha units like [[Swimmer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Butterfly]] will do the job just fine. When the boss wave starts, focus on consistantly sending out meatshields while you slowly chip down the Dober using your Crazed units as well as the help of a backliner like [[Ururun Wolf (Special Cat)|Ururun]] or any Ubers you may happen to own. Rinse and repeat for the second Dober, and you've won.

Alternatively, if you happen to have [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut]], you can pin the Dober to the base, use him to murder the Dober, and then rack up insane amounts of damage to kill Cat Kart.


